## ⚠️ 3. Non-Negotiable Rules to Prevent Disqualification

1. **Strict Time Limits**:
   - 240-second videos that hit 241 seconds get **cut off**, not excused. Stick to the ~450-word script.
   - The 30-second global video must stay **under 30.0 seconds**.
2. **Under-18 Safety Rule**:
   - Recognizable names, voices, or faces of anyone under the age of 18 **must not appear** in any video or photo submission. Use adult team members or synthetic avatar voices.
3. **NASA Data Must Be Spoken Aloud**:
   - In Video 2, judges specifically check if NASA open datasets are named out loud on camera. Do not rely solely on on-screen text.
4. **Incognito Link Test**:
   - Test your GitHub link and YouTube video links in an **Incognito / Private Window** before submitting. If a judge sees a "Private Video" or "Sign-in Required" screen, the project cannot be scored.
5. **Two Separate Registrations**:
   - Ensure the team is fully registered on **both** the Bangladesh local form ([nasaspaceappsbd.com](https://www.nasaspaceappsbd.com/)) and the global NASA site ([spaceappschallenge.org](https://spaceappschallenge.org)).
